Panel C:

This should be three small network figures where nodes are resources and edges
are overlaps between them (scaled to edge tickness). Node sizes represent the
number of entities in the resource. We should make 3 of these plots: Molecular
entites, Interactions, Literature references. Making these plots have three
challenges: the size scales should be tuned with care to remain readable but
avoid miniature or huge nodes and edges; below certain value to edges should be
removed, we should show only a reasonable density of the thickest edges; the
layout and labeling should be optimized for an even distribution of the nodes
to avoid overlaps (same layout should be applied for all 3 plots). Igraph is
able to create such figures. There is an idea that we could show major classes
of molecular entities as pie charts inside the nodes, though this would mean we
can not have too small nodes, and the creation of such figure is technically
challenging.

Panel D:

This could be a barplot with 4 or more facets vertically. The facets would be major
entity types: Proteins, Metabolites, Lipids, Drugs, maybe we can add further
categories. The y-axis of the barplots should show number of interactions.
While each bar should be an interaction type category, such as Signaling,
TF-target, Allosteric regulation, Transport, Ligand-receptor, Drug-target.

Panel E:

This would be a panel about the level of structural specificity vs. major
categories of chemicals. The vertical facets could be the categories: lipids, amino acid
metabolism, nucleic acid metabolism, carbohydrates, drugs, food compounds,
xenobiotics, (think if you can find more categories). Each facet contains a
barplot, with the levels of structural specificity on the x-axis: see these in
the description of panel A. Because the stereo specific structures might be
orders or magnitudes more numerous than the others, we might need log scale,
but then maybe the other columns will be all similar heights, this we'll see.

Panel F:

Comparison with RaMP: using our database, analyse RaMP: when one RaMP ID points
to different structures (InChI keys), in each of those cases, what is the
reason, what is the level of difference between those structures? Only
stereochemistry, tautomery, different level of structural specificity, somewhat
similar structures, totally different structures? Quantify these cases and plot
them on a simple bar plot.

